    <p>Here $o_i$ is candidate op number $i$, and $\alpha_i$ is its architecture weight, a learnable number that says how much the search currently likes that op. Softmax over $\alpha$ turns the likes into blending weights. During the search every op runs and the block outputs the weighted mixture. At the end you keep the op with the biggest $\alpha$ and throw away the rest. The trick is: replace a hard choice with a soft average, optimize it with gradients, then harden it.</p>
 
